    "message": "Desktop shell: the macOS dmg smoke exits on its own snapshot\n\nThe `macos-universal (dmg)` job built and imaged correctly on v6.45.2 and\nthen failed on the smoke's second line, before a single assertion ran.\n\n`smoke/macos-dmg.sh` runs under `set -euo pipefail`. Its snapshot helper\nlists `/Applications` and `~/Applications`; a runner has no\n`~/Applications`, so `ls` exits 2, `2>/dev/null` hides the message but not\nthe status, and a failing command inside a pipeline is a failing pipeline.\n`snapshot > \"$before\"` therefore ended the script with exit 1 and no\noutput beyond the image's digest.\n\nTwo more instances of the same class, found while fixing it:\n\n  * `read_key` is `defaults read ... 2>/dev/null`, which exits non-zero for\n    a key that is absent -- and an assignment whose command substitution\n    fails ends the script under `set -e`, so a missing plist key would have\n    produced a silent exit instead of the named assertion two lines below;\n  * the `Authority=` extraction piped `sed` into `head -n 1`, which can\n    close the pipe early and make the whole substitution non-zero. `sed`\n    already prints nothing when there is no authority, which is the case\n    this asserts, so `head` was never needed.\n\nA contract test pins the snapshot guards and `read_key`, because this is\nnot a bug anyone re-reads a script and notices; it is one you only see on\na machine that lacks the directory.\n\nNo version bump: the wheel is unaffected and v6.45.2 is already published.\nRe-dispatch the shell build against that tag with `-f ref=main`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT",
